{title: 231 - Blest Be the King}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #231 • STOKESAY CASTLE • 7.6.7.6.6.8.7.6}
{lyricist: Fred Pratt Green}
{composer: Eric H. Thiman}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 231}
{meta: tune STOKESAY CASTLE}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.6.6.8.7.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Blest [C]be the King [Em]whose coming
[C]Is in [G]the [Em]name of God!
[Dm]For Him [C]let doors be [Dm]opened,
[G]No hearts [Am]against [G]Him barred!
[Am]Not robed [Em/B]in [Dm]royal [Em/B]splendor,
[Am]In power [G]and pomp [Am]comes [Dm]He;
[Em/B]But clad [C]as [G]are [A#]the poorest,
[G7/F]Such His humility.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Blest [C]be the King [Em]whose coming
[C]Is in [G]the [Em]name of God!
[Dm]By those [C]who truly [Dm]listen
[G]His voice [Am]is truly [G]heard;
[Am]Pity [Em/B]the [Dm]proud and [Em/B]haughty,
[Am]Who have [G]not learned [Am]to heed
[Em/B]The Christ [C]who [G]is [A#]the promise,
[G7/F]Who has atonement made.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Blest [C]be the King [Em]whose coming
[C]Is in [G]the [Em]name of God!
[Dm]He only [C]to the [Dm]humble
[G]Reveals [Am]the face [G]of God.
[Am]All power [Em/B]is [Dm]His, [Em/B]all glory!
[Am]All things [G]are in [Am]His hand,
[Em/B]All ages [G]and [A#]all peoples,
[G7/F]'Till time itself shall end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Blest [C]be the King [Em]whose coming
[C]Is in [G]the [Em]name of God!
[Dm]He offers [C]to the [Dm]burdened
[G]The rest [Am]and grace [G]they need.
[Am]Gentle [Em/B]is [Dm]He and [Em/B]humble!
[Am]And light [G]his Yoke [Am]shall be,
[Em/B]For He [C]would [G]have [A#]us bear [Am]it,
[G7/F]So He can made us free!
{end_of_verse}
